(PRC-06 — `Remove the directory called '<path>'.` performs rmdir(2).
 Also covers: PRC-07 (`Delete` works as well as `Remove`) and PRC-08
 (`the` and `called` are both optional — all four combinations parse).
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-06.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   Remove directory removed it
   Remove the directory removed it
   Delete directory called removed it
   Delete the directory called removed it
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_one".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_two".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_three".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_four".
Remove directory "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_one".
Remove the directory "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_two".
Delete directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_three".
Delete the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_four".
If "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_one" is not available then, print "Remove directory removed it".
If "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_two" is not available then, print "Remove the directory removed it".
If "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_three" is not available then, print "Delete directory called removed it".
If "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_four" is not available then, print "Delete the directory called removed it".
